**Definition 1.2 (source quantities).** Use source amplitudes
$h_0,h_1,h_2,a,b,c_{\rm src},d>0$, with $m_1,m_2>0$, and set

$$
\begin{gathered}
D=\operatorname{diag}(h_0,h_1,h_2),\quad
T=ae_0e_1^T+be_1e_0^T,\quad
S=c_{\rm src}e_0e_2^T+de_2e_0^T,\quad
M=\operatorname{diag}(0,m_1,m_2),\\
D^\dagger D+T^\dagger T+S^\dagger S+M=I_3,\quad
\theta=\frac{ab}{h_0h_1},\quad
\omega=\frac{c_{\rm src}d}{h_0h_2},\quad
\delta=\theta+\omega\in(0,1),\\
s_0=\sqrt\delta,\qquad \alpha=\theta/\delta,\qquad
\beta=\omega/\delta,\qquad \alpha+\beta=1.
\end{gathered}
\tag{FC.1}
$$

The vectors $e_i$ in (FC.1) are qutrit coordinate vectors. The source
is one consistent root; a rectangular enclosure of its coordinates
does not assert TP at other points. Let
$\Delta=\rho_{27,+,+}-\rho_{5,+,+}$ in the original supported input
coordinates of GC. Put $K_0=D,K_1=T,K_2=S$,
$N_{ij}=\operatorname{tr}(K_i\Delta K_j^\dagger)$,
$L=\operatorname{diag}(s_0,1,1)$, $G=LNL$ and
$H_0=(1-\delta)N_{00}>0$. For $h=(1,z,w)$ on
$\alpha z^2+\beta w^2=1$ define

$$
\begin{gathered}
K_h=s_0D+zT+wS,\quad n_h=(0,dw/h_2,-bz/h_1)^T,\\
\ell(h)=h^TGh,\quad f(h)=n_h^T\Delta n_h,\\
\mathfrak c(h)=
\frac{h_1^2h_2^2\delta+a^2h_2^2z^2+c_{\rm src}^2h_1^2w^2}
     {h_0^2\delta+b^2z^2+d^2w^2}>0,\\
V=\frac{m_2h_1^2}{b^2},\quad W=\frac{m_1h_2^2}{d^2},\quad
\mu=\alpha V+\beta W,\quad u_F=V/\mu,\quad v_F=W/\mu,\\
\mathfrak c_f=\mathfrak c(1,\sqrt{u_F},\sqrt{v_F}),\quad
\nu=\mu/\mathfrak c_f,\quad t_0=W/\mathfrak c_f.
\end{gathered}
\tag{FC.2}
$$

In particular $\alpha,\beta>0$ and $t_0>0$. These are GC's physical
quantities, including its failure pairing; no freely fitted payoff or
failure allocation is substituted.

